  "hostNotes": "Be generous: the prompt is 'might spot', so introduced animals, dogs on the beach, rock-pool critters, fish and offshore whales all count, and any genuine Otways species not in this list scores as deep. Generic answers (bird, snake, possum, wallaby, shark) are separate entries from the species, so a specific name is the better play. Traps: goanna/lace monitor, emu, dingo, red kangaroo, wallaroo, Tasmanian devil, crocodile and box jellyfish do not occur here (reject or allow a re-answer); 'drop bear' is a koala, 'crow' is a raven, 'crayfish' means rock lobster not yabby, and 'human' or 'bunyip' is the host's call."
